      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3210667895,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Also, from a quick look at the tip-of-main-branch libssh:\n\n1. code using libssh can install its own logger function;\n2. the default logger prints to the standard error a string that includes a date and the severity code.\n\nI don't know if it'd be worth it to have extcaps add their own logger that uses `ws_log()` and mapping libssh severity codes to `ws_log()` severity codes; a map might be:\n\n- `SSH_LOG_WARN` -> `LOG_LEVEL_WARNING`;\n- `SSH_LOG_INFO` -> `LOG_LEVEL_INFO`;\n- `SSH_LOG_DEBUG` -> `LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG`;\n- `SSH_LOG_TRACE` -> `LOG_LEVEL_NOISY`.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-03-31T19:39:15.875Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-03-31T21:35:49.313Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 468842003,
